    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0766" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg616"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3691/48.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs of
                            Salvador to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic">February 12,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have had the honor to receive the transcript your excellency was pleased to
                    send me of President Roosevelt’s telegram to the Presidents <pb facs="0767"
                        n="617" xml:id="pg617"/> of Honduras and Nicaragua interposing his good
                    offices to the end of obtaining a pacific settlement of the difficulties pending
                    between the two Republics, and I am glad to inform your excellency that
                    President Escalon once more addressed Presidents Bonilla and Zelaya to-day,
                    tendering them again his friendly mediation to that purpose.</p>
                <p>With the highest consideration,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel Delgardos.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
